## Interpretation
On this 10-image corpus, chunk-5 produces byte-identical output to W11-1 — the
8 screenshots in the calibration set all have c_needed_lossless < 0.35 < 0.45,
so both gates admit. The chunk-5 win is structural: the gate is 22% tighter at
C=0.35 vs W11-1's C=0.45 against more-accurate (lossless-shape) overhead, so
pathological mixed content where xyb-overshoot was admitting a marginal patch
(c_needed_xyb in (0.35, 0.45]) will now be rejected. That regression-protection
band doesn't intersect the gb82-sc corpus.
